Thus we need to avoid setting destination leg loaded. So we should not use assemble_fully_loaded_leg or assemble_destination_loaded_leg. Use assemble_transport_leg.

Now we also need candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta. There are several establish_clearance actions: nominal, origin_loaded, destination_loaded, full_load. They require candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, and certain leg loaded flags. For nominal: requires not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded. For origin_loaded: requires origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded. For destination_loaded: requires not origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded. For full_load: requires both loaded.

Thus after we have loading container loaded and linked, but origin leg not loaded, destination leg not loaded (if we used assemble_transport_leg), we can use establish_clearance_nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, compliance linked, loading container linked, loading container leg linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). Effect: candidate_clearance_established and route_sequence_context_set.

Thus we can achieve clearance via nominal.

Now we need candidate_finalized shift_candidate_beta. There are two finalize actions: finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete, not candidate_finalized) effect candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready. Or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized) effect candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready. Or finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized) effect candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready.

We already will have candidate_clearance_established and route_sequence_context_set after establish_clearance_nominal. So we could use finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation which requires route_sequence_validated. Or we could use finalize_candidate_direct which requires candidate_clearance_established and not route_sequence_context_set. But after establish_clearance_nominal we get route_sequence_context_set true, so finalize_candidate_direct not applicable (requires not route_sequence_context_set). So we need either finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (needs compliance_validation_complete) or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (needs route_sequence_validated). We have compliance_validation_complete for shift_candidate_alpha only; not for beta. We can maybe achieve compliance_validation_complete for beta via verify_compliance_certificate (requires operator_alignment_confirmed, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, not compliance_validation_complete). So we need to have operator_alignment_confirmed for beta (we will assign operator) and compliance certificate linked (we will assign). Then we can verify_compliance_certificate to set compliance_validation_complete. Then we can finalize via finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation.

Alternatively we could validate route sequence (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, candidate_service_window_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_destination_availability_linked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, candidate_task_profile_linked, not route_sequence_validated). Effect: route_sequence_validated.

We will have candidate_clearance_established and route_sequence_context_set after establish_clearance_nominal. We need to attach service window to shift_candidate_beta (service_window_available). We have service_window_alpha and beta available. We'll need to attach service_window to candidate (attach_service_window action requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, service_window_available). Effect: candidate_service_window_linked, not service_window_available.

We also need candidate_origin_availability_linked and candidate_destination_availability_linked (already true). Need origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (we will get via load/unload). Need candidate_task_profile_linked (we will attach). Then we can validate route sequence.

Thus we can finalize via finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation after we have route_sequence_validated.

Alternatively we could get compliance_validation_complete via verify_compliance_certificate and then finalize via finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. Either works.

We also need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta (goal). We can achieve via verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_loading_verified). So after we have staged, linked operator and skill certificate, we can verify loading profile.

Thus overall plan steps:

1. Prepare origin_availability_alpha:
   - attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   - confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha

2. Prepare destination_availability_alpha:
   - allocate vehicle_unit_beta to destination_availability_alpha (allocate_vehicle_unit)
   - attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   - confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha

3. Load and unload cargo at origin to get origin_node_occupied & ready and origin_availability_confirmed & locked.
   - load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   - unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha

   (Note: unload_origin_payload requires candidate_prepared, candidate_task_profile_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_occupied, origin_payload_linked, not origin_availability_confirmed. After load we have origin_node_occupied, origin_availability_locked, origin_payload_linked, cargo not available. Then unload requires origin_node_occupied, origin_payload_linked, not origin_availability_confirmed (we have not confirmed yet). Good.)

4. Load and unload cargo at destination to get destination_node_occupied & ready and destination_availability_confirmed & locked.
   - load_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   - unload_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha

   (Note: load_destination_payload requires candidate_prepared, destination_availability_node_linked, cargo_available, not destination_availability_locked. After previous steps, cargo_available is true again (since we unloaded origin). Destination_availability_locked? Not yet. So we can load. After load: destination_node_occupied, destination_availability_locked, destination_payload_linked, cargo not available. Then unload requires destination_node_occupied, destination_payload_linked, not destination_availability_confirmed (we have not confirmed yet). After unload: destination_node_ready, destination_availability_confirmed, cargo_available, not destination_payload_linked.)

Now we have origin and destination availability confirmed and locked, nodes occupied and ready.

5. Prepare shift_candidate_beta:
